WEBVTT

00:34.121 --> 00:37.646
♪ Your love is king♪

00:37.689 --> 00:39.909
♪ Crown you in my heart♪

00:39.909 --> 00:43.521
♪ Your love is king♪

00:43.565 --> 00:45.088
♪ Never need to part♪

00:45.132 --> 00:49.179
♪ Your kisses ring...♪

00:49.223 --> 00:51.790
Feel like we should maybe
slow down a little bit.

00:51.790 --> 00:54.010
♪ Touching the very part of me♪

00:54.010 --> 00:56.186
♪ It's making my soul sing♪

00:56.230 --> 00:59.015
♪ Tearing the very heart
of me...♪

00:59.015 --> 01:01.539
Supposed to be a turn-off soon.

01:01.583 --> 01:03.324
♪ Your love is king...♪

01:03.367 --> 01:06.022
You don't think we missed it?

01:06.022 --> 01:07.502
Nah, I think we're good.

01:09.808 --> 01:12.028
♪ You're the ruler of my heart♪

01:12.028 --> 01:13.725
♪ Your kisses ring...♪

01:13.725 --> 01:15.336
Here he is.

01:15.379 --> 01:17.077
♪ Round and round
and round my.♪

01:26.173 --> 01:28.000
Hey, Earn.

01:28.044 --> 01:30.394
- Welcome, welcome. You made it.
- Thank you, thank you.

01:30.481 --> 01:31.961
Hey, I'm gonna ask
that you come down here

01:32.048 --> 01:33.702
at five miles per hour.

01:33.745 --> 01:35.617
You know, there's kids and dogs
running around,

01:35.617 --> 01:36.835
sometimes deer.

01:36.922 --> 01:39.360
Yeah, yeah. Sorry.

01:39.403 --> 01:41.623
So, when you pass this road,

01:41.623 --> 01:42.841
just look on either side
for signs

01:42.928 --> 01:44.234
to point you
where you need to go.

01:44.278 --> 01:45.409
I got you booked
for entire grounds.

01:45.496 --> 01:47.237
Great.

01:47.281 --> 01:49.718
- Oh, is that the birthday girl?
- Yeah,

01:49.761 --> 01:52.547
that's-that's Lottie.
This is Van.

01:52.547 --> 01:54.418
Hi.

01:54.505 --> 01:57.247
Beautiful family.
Well, I hope y'all enjoy.

01:57.291 --> 02:01.425
Need anything, don't hesitate
to holler at me or my wife.

02:01.425 --> 02:03.035
- Thank you, bye.
- All right, thank you.

02:03.079 --> 02:04.341
Happy birthday.

02:08.998 --> 02:10.347
- Very nice.
- Yeah.

02:12.654 --> 02:14.395
Here, you want
to carry one of these?

02:14.438 --> 02:17.528
Take the best one.

02:17.572 --> 02:19.443
Ooh, purple.

02:19.443 --> 02:21.141
That's Prince's favorite color.

02:24.753 --> 02:26.102
What do you think
are the chances that

02:26.102 --> 02:28.583
that guy's gonna
kill us in our sleep?

02:28.583 --> 02:30.237
Honestly?

02:32.761 --> 02:34.154
Eight.
Eight percent.

02:36.156 --> 02:37.722
You think eight percent?

02:39.159 --> 02:40.943
Sounds high.

02:50.953 --> 02:52.041
It's a big tarp.

02:52.128 --> 02:54.478
Yeah.

02:54.565 --> 02:55.740
I got, uh...

02:57.481 --> 03:00.789
I got a really awesome tent.

03:00.832 --> 03:03.357
It's, like,
the most expensive one in REI.

03:03.357 --> 03:06.360
The... the guy was like,
this is the best one they had.

03:06.360 --> 03:09.145
Like, uh, I think
it's, like, a 12-person.

03:09.189 --> 03:11.103
Like, uh...

03:11.147 --> 03:12.714
It's for how many people?

03:12.714 --> 03:15.151
12 person, and you can
split the rooms,

03:15.195 --> 03:16.718
and it has, like, a porch, too.

03:16.805 --> 03:19.677
We're gonna be freezing.

03:19.721 --> 03:21.375
What?

03:23.638 --> 03:25.901
'Cause if you don't have
enough body heat to insulate

03:25.944 --> 03:28.512
the... space...

03:28.599 --> 03:29.861
It'll be fine, though.

03:31.298 --> 03:33.125
Okay.

03:33.169 --> 03:34.518
- It'll be fine.
I'm-I'm excited.
- I'm-I'm sorry.

03:34.605 --> 03:37.042
- No, no, no. Okay.
- I didn't know.

03:37.086 --> 03:39.828
- It looks really nice. I mean...
- Okay. You're...

03:39.871 --> 03:41.743
very welcome.

03:41.830 --> 03:44.093
We're gonna... I'm gonna get...

03:44.093 --> 03:46.617
It's kind of big.

03:46.704 --> 03:48.663
- Let's find the corners.
- Hey, Lottie, you want
to-you want to help us?

03:48.750 --> 03:50.317
No.

03:53.537 --> 03:55.409
Huh.

03:55.452 --> 03:57.280
What's going on with her?

03:57.324 --> 03:59.021
She's just tired.

04:00.544 --> 04:01.980
She'll be fine.

04:34.926 --> 04:36.537
Can you hand me those?

04:36.580 --> 04:38.147
Um, this?

04:38.147 --> 04:39.104
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

04:39.148 --> 04:40.367
No problem.

04:48.375 --> 04:49.941
So, have you...

04:50.028 --> 04:52.379
thought more about L.A.?

04:59.473 --> 05:00.822
I mean...

05:02.737 --> 05:05.392
Yeah, I've thought
about it a lot, actually.

05:12.921 --> 05:14.314
We were gonna talk about it
a little later.

05:17.491 --> 05:20.407
Yeah.
Whenever you want.

05:27.065 --> 05:30.155
Those ones, I think,
go by the door.

05:33.724 --> 05:34.551
Hmm.

05:36.771 --> 05:37.989
Are we missing a pole?

05:40.340 --> 05:43.212
Doesn't quite look right.

05:44.866 --> 05:46.433
What do you think?

05:52.656 --> 05:53.918
She loves it.

05:56.443 --> 05:58.401
Which room you gonna sleep in?

05:58.445 --> 05:59.968
Hm... this one.

06:00.011 --> 06:02.187
Ooh.

06:02.231 --> 06:04.407
Which one's Daddy
gonna sleep in?

06:04.451 --> 06:05.669
He can sleep outside.

06:05.713 --> 06:08.150
Outside?

06:10.892 --> 06:12.459
I'll get my toothbrush.

06:56.285 --> 06:58.113
I peed.

06:58.156 --> 07:00.724
That's great.

07:00.811 --> 07:02.552
That's exactly what
we were supposed to do.

07:30.624 --> 07:32.321
This river's too high.

07:34.628 --> 07:37.413
- We can't cross it.
- I think we can...

07:37.413 --> 07:38.849
We can make it across here.

07:38.893 --> 07:41.199
I think there's a lo-log
underneath there.

07:41.243 --> 07:43.550
We could hop to that rock.

07:43.550 --> 07:46.640
Oh... you think
she can cross that?

07:46.683 --> 07:48.990
We're just gonna get wet.

07:48.990 --> 07:51.427
- It's too high.
- We'll get wet up to here, but

07:51.514 --> 07:53.385
- she can get on my shoulders.
- Earn. No.

07:53.429 --> 07:54.517
She can get on my shoulders.

07:54.561 --> 07:55.475
Come on, Lottie, let's go.

07:57.694 --> 08:00.436
We can't cross this.

08:00.436 --> 08:02.264
- You don't think so?
- No.

08:05.572 --> 08:08.357
- Maybe...
- That... that-that's
all gonna collapse.

08:08.357 --> 08:09.706
It's all gonna collapse.

08:28.246 --> 08:30.466
That's not true.

08:30.510 --> 08:32.599
- Is it?
- Not in Europe.

08:32.686 --> 08:34.383
- All right.
- It's hard there.

08:42.043 --> 08:43.174
You enjoying
your birthday, Lottie?

08:45.263 --> 08:47.178
Do we have any other snacks?

08:47.265 --> 08:50.704
Yeah, I think we do.

08:50.704 --> 08:52.183
- It's like I'm not here.
- I don't really like
my birthday.

08:53.968 --> 08:55.535
Since when?

08:59.060 --> 09:01.932
What kind of six-year-old
doesn't enjoy their birthday?

09:01.932 --> 09:03.847
You know how she is
when she's in her moods.

09:07.372 --> 09:09.200
You can't catch anything?

09:11.855 --> 09:14.292
Don't worry, we're gonna go
catch fish later,

09:14.292 --> 09:17.861
and then tonight we're
gonna try to catch a snipe.

09:17.948 --> 09:19.602
A snipe?

09:19.646 --> 09:21.735
Yeah.
We're gonna go snipe hunting.

09:21.778 --> 09:23.824
What's a snipe?

09:23.867 --> 09:26.391
It's this really rare creature.

09:26.435 --> 09:28.393
It's nearly extinct.

09:28.437 --> 09:29.960
And it only comes out at night

09:30.004 --> 09:33.050
when the moon is out,
and it's really crazy long,

09:33.094 --> 09:35.400
and it has red eyes.

09:35.444 --> 09:38.273
But only the coolest
and the smartest can catch it.

09:38.316 --> 09:40.101
Did you ever catch it?

09:40.188 --> 09:42.103
No, but maybe
with your help I can.

09:42.103 --> 09:44.192
I want to catch it.

09:44.235 --> 09:45.715
Yeah, we're gonna try.

09:50.981 --> 09:52.635
Are y...

09:52.679 --> 09:53.941
are you pranking our daughter?

09:55.638 --> 09:57.684
You don't know
what a snipe hunt is?

09:57.771 --> 09:59.337
- No.
- It's, like, a tradition.

09:59.337 --> 10:01.209
I did it at Girl Scouts.

10:01.252 --> 10:02.471
You were in Girl Scouts?

10:02.558 --> 10:04.516
- I did not know that.
- Yeah.

10:04.560 --> 10:06.997
I did it for just a summer,
when I was eight.

10:07.041 --> 10:09.086
I didn't like being trapped
camping with people

10:09.130 --> 10:11.915
I didn't vibe with, so...

10:54.392 --> 10:57.178
...I think, is actually a bird

10:57.265 --> 10:59.833
that's hard to catch,
or something like that,

10:59.920 --> 11:01.704
and it turned
into this folklore,

11:01.748 --> 11:03.837
so, you could, in the end,

11:03.880 --> 11:05.099
we could tell her it's a bird.

11:05.186 --> 11:06.404
Okay.

11:07.971 --> 11:09.843
- You want to...
- I have no problem with

11:09.843 --> 11:12.062
doing it. It sounds... sounds
like it could be, uh, fun.

11:12.106 --> 11:14.848
You know, cool,
it's just, when you-when you

11:14.848 --> 11:16.545
- first hear "snipe hunt"...
- Mm-hmm.

11:16.545 --> 11:18.634
it sounds like a racist,

11:18.721 --> 11:20.767
- like, mob.
- Oh, my God.

11:20.767 --> 11:23.204
Like, "Let's get the snipe.

11:23.204 --> 11:25.554
- You're so silly.
- He's taking our jobs."

11:25.641 --> 11:27.164
Hey!

11:27.208 --> 11:28.513
Oh.

11:28.557 --> 11:30.994
- Lottie. You...
- Wow.

11:30.994 --> 11:33.388
- Maybe put him down.
- Yeah, put him down.

11:33.431 --> 11:34.563
- Yeah, maybe put him dow...
- I don't want to, though.

11:34.650 --> 11:38.610
Lottie.
This is nature, okay?

11:38.654 --> 11:42.614
That toad is not for you, okay?

11:42.658 --> 11:44.616
I want to hold it, though.

11:44.660 --> 11:45.661
- I want it to stay.
- Yeah.

11:45.748 --> 11:47.794
But it let you
take a look at him,

11:47.794 --> 11:50.448
and then it wanted to go.

11:50.535 --> 11:54.409
You should feel lucky that
you got to hold it, okay?

11:54.452 --> 11:56.324
Come on.
I have some raspberries.

11:56.367 --> 11:57.717
Come on.

12:03.113 --> 12:05.028
You know, I know
this little girl.

12:05.028 --> 12:08.597
Her name is, uh, Shottie.

12:08.684 --> 12:10.599
And, um,

12:10.686 --> 12:13.776
she has a dad named Shmad.

12:13.820 --> 12:16.561
And, um...

12:16.605 --> 12:18.389
all they do is eat ice cream

12:18.476 --> 12:20.609
in Opposite World.

12:20.609 --> 12:22.829
What?

12:22.829 --> 12:24.265
All they do is eat ice cream,

12:24.265 --> 12:25.919
and they get thinner.

12:25.962 --> 12:28.443
That's, like,
totally the opposite

12:28.486 --> 12:30.706
of what you're supposed to do.

12:30.706 --> 12:31.620
- What would be the...
- You're sup...

12:31.707 --> 12:33.709
you're supposed to not have

12:33.796 --> 12:35.667
- Ice cream.
- ice cream all the time,

12:35.711 --> 12:38.409
and when you do,
you're supposed to get fat.

12:38.496 --> 12:40.716
- Really?
- Yeah.

12:40.760 --> 12:42.283
Is that why I'm so fat?

12:42.370 --> 12:45.025
I eat ice cream,
like, every day.

12:45.068 --> 12:46.287
Like, for breakfast.

12:46.287 --> 12:48.028
- No, you don't.
- I do.

12:52.510 --> 12:54.164
You guys good?

12:54.208 --> 12:55.383
- Yeah, we're good.
- Yeah.

12:55.426 --> 12:56.950
All right.

12:57.037 --> 13:00.127
- I love how calm it is.
- Yeah, it's great.

13:00.170 --> 13:01.302
- Oh, that
actually is cool.
- It's really cool.

13:11.616 --> 13:13.880
I wish grandma
and grandpa were here.

13:17.753 --> 13:19.233
Hmm.

13:21.844 --> 13:24.847
- Yeah, that makes sense.
- Yeah.

13:24.891 --> 13:27.850
You know, we'll make sure
that, um,

13:27.894 --> 13:30.331
they celebrate with us
this weekend.

13:30.331 --> 13:31.419
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

13:31.462 --> 13:33.421
Are you just missing them

13:33.508 --> 13:35.292
or you wish they were doing
your birthday with you?

13:35.336 --> 13:36.119
- Both.
- Both.

13:36.163 --> 13:37.381
Both.

13:40.689 --> 13:42.778
Well, I think it's...

13:42.865 --> 13:45.085
kind of cool that we're all...

13:45.128 --> 13:47.435
- Together. Yeah.
- together. Yeah.

13:47.478 --> 13:49.219
That's special.

13:49.263 --> 13:50.786
That's special, too, right?
I mean,

13:50.873 --> 13:52.701
- it doesn't happen all the time.
- Mm-hmm.

13:52.701 --> 13:54.050
Yeah.

14:13.722 --> 14:15.332
Am I starving,

14:15.376 --> 14:18.031
or is this incredible?

14:18.074 --> 14:20.076
It's really good.

14:25.168 --> 14:26.953
I think we should
talk more about L.A.

14:29.825 --> 14:33.133
Yeah.
We probably should.

14:33.176 --> 14:34.525
Mom.

14:34.525 --> 14:37.137
The moon is out.

14:37.180 --> 14:39.095
Oh, it is.

14:41.489 --> 14:44.927
Baby, why don't we go looking
for snipes tomorrow, hm?

14:44.971 --> 14:45.885
I think it's a little late now.

14:55.633 --> 14:57.635
Here, take the pillowcase,

14:57.722 --> 14:59.637
put it on the ground,
and open it up.

14:59.681 --> 15:02.379
Do you have a marshmallow?

15:02.423 --> 15:04.729
- Just one?
- Yeah.

15:04.773 --> 15:07.080
And you're gonna take
the marshmallow,

15:07.080 --> 15:08.864
you're gonna put it
inside the pillowcase

15:08.951 --> 15:11.649
all the way to the end, okay?

15:11.736 --> 15:14.174
Now, you're gonna
take the lantern,

15:14.217 --> 15:16.176
you're gonna put it
next to the opening,

15:16.219 --> 15:18.221
so that when the snipe walks in,
you can see it.

15:19.744 --> 15:22.399
You need to find a stick. Here.

15:22.443 --> 15:24.924
And then you're gonna
make this sound.

15:27.230 --> 15:29.145
That's gonna lure
the snipe, okay?

15:30.973 --> 15:32.757
And the snipe should just
walk in on its own

15:32.801 --> 15:34.672
to get the marshmallow bait.

15:34.672 --> 15:36.892
You know what you're
gonna do when it does that?

15:36.892 --> 15:39.199
You're gonna take your foot,

15:39.242 --> 15:41.288
you're gonna stomp
on the pillowcase,

15:41.331 --> 15:42.245
trap the snipe in there,
and then you're gonna

15:42.332 --> 15:44.465
hit it on the head, okay?

15:44.465 --> 15:45.901
Okay.

15:45.945 --> 15:47.163
Here.

15:49.035 --> 15:51.167
Good job.
All right, baby, have fun.

15:53.256 --> 15:55.258
Where are you going?

15:55.258 --> 15:58.435
Aw. Baby, you have to
hunt the snipe alone.

15:58.479 --> 15:59.436
If there's
too many people around,

15:59.480 --> 16:01.090
the snipe's not gonna come.

16:01.134 --> 16:03.484
But don't worry,
we're right over there, okay?

16:33.644 --> 16:35.211
What?

16:37.300 --> 16:39.085
You, what?

16:42.653 --> 16:44.568
L.A.

16:46.962 --> 16:48.224
You gonna come with me?

16:51.532 --> 16:53.012
Is that why you did all this?

16:54.317 --> 16:55.449
What do you mean?

16:58.060 --> 16:59.627
You know, it feels
a little manipulative

16:59.670 --> 17:02.021
to rent out
an entire campground.

17:07.200 --> 17:09.898
I-I just wanted to make
Lottie's birthday special.

17:22.128 --> 17:23.259
Can I ask you a question?

17:26.915 --> 17:29.265
What's so great about Atlanta...

17:31.572 --> 17:33.269
...that you can't
leave it behind?

17:37.578 --> 17:40.885
I mean, it'd be
my choice to stay.

17:40.929 --> 17:44.019
That's not what
it's about, though.

17:44.063 --> 17:47.414
I'm afraid that...

17:47.457 --> 17:50.243
it's about you not wanting
to be alone when you go there,

17:50.286 --> 17:52.593
and that you're scared of that.

17:52.680 --> 17:55.378
And I'm... not just
your security blanket.

18:01.732 --> 18:02.820
Got him!

18:02.864 --> 18:04.822
What?

18:04.866 --> 18:08.261
I got the snipe.

18:08.304 --> 18:11.481
Uh... what did it look like?

18:11.568 --> 18:15.006
Long, with red eyes,
and I hit it with the stick

18:15.050 --> 18:16.138
when I caught it.

18:16.182 --> 18:18.706
Uh, okay, okay,

18:18.749 --> 18:20.577
Lottie, um...

18:20.621 --> 18:22.188
listen.

18:22.188 --> 18:24.277
When I count to three,

18:24.364 --> 18:27.367
you're going to put
the lamp down very slowly,

18:27.410 --> 18:29.412
drop the bag,
and run to Mommy, okay?

18:29.412 --> 18:32.154
- Okay.
- Okay.

18:32.198 --> 18:36.027
One, two...

18:36.071 --> 18:37.638
- three. Come, come, come,
come, come, come, come,
- Go, go, go, go,

18:37.725 --> 18:38.987
- go, go.
- Come, come, come.

18:39.074 --> 18:41.120
Baby, are you okay?

18:43.687 --> 18:45.211
Hold this.

18:46.647 --> 18:49.650
Earn...

18:49.737 --> 18:52.218
- Please be careful.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

19:07.015 --> 19:08.799
- Aah!
- Oh, my God.

19:08.799 --> 19:10.192
Oh! Oh!

19:10.236 --> 19:12.977
- What was that?
- What was that?

19:13.021 --> 19:14.805
It was a snipe.

19:14.805 --> 19:17.286
I got him.

19:23.684 --> 19:25.033
VAN and EARN:
♪ Happy birth...♪

19:25.033 --> 19:27.296
Shh! No singing, please.

19:38.133 --> 19:40.048
Happy birthday, baby.

19:40.135 --> 19:43.617
Happy birthday. so big.

20:24.745 --> 20:26.747
Earn.

20:26.790 --> 20:29.315
Yeah?

20:29.315 --> 20:32.883
Is that your teeth chattering?

20:32.883 --> 20:34.320
Maybe.

20:36.104 --> 20:38.759
I... I think you should
just get in with us.

20:38.759 --> 20:40.456
This is really sad.

21:08.919 --> 21:10.921
Her feet are cold.

21:10.921 --> 21:13.576
- Her feet?
- Yeah.

21:13.663 --> 21:16.100
Yeah...

21:16.144 --> 21:17.798
It's those sharp toenails.

21:17.841 --> 21:19.930
I know. Talons.

21:32.595 --> 21:33.509
Lottie?

21:36.730 --> 21:39.123
Lottie, do you want
some more s'mores?

21:39.167 --> 21:42.388
What are you doing?

21:42.388 --> 21:44.825
Testing to see if she's awake.

21:53.747 --> 21:56.271
You know, when I go...

21:58.621 --> 22:01.450
...I-I wouldn't
have to be alone.

22:04.758 --> 22:07.282
You know, I'm not...

22:07.282 --> 22:09.806
I'm not saying that to be cocky.

22:09.850 --> 22:11.939
I have a good job, and a...

22:11.982 --> 22:14.071
cool job.

22:14.115 --> 22:16.509
I'm not terrible-looking.

22:18.511 --> 22:20.251
And I'm not tied to anything

22:20.295 --> 22:21.644
that would
turn someone off from me.

22:23.733 --> 22:26.170
And you'd be here,
raising our kid.

22:26.214 --> 22:28.956
And I'd see you every, you know,

22:28.999 --> 22:31.350
couple of months,
maybe once or twice a year.

22:33.308 --> 22:36.093
If I didn't want to be alone,

22:36.137 --> 22:38.095
I wouldn't have to be.

22:38.182 --> 22:39.227
I could find someone.

22:41.185 --> 22:43.100
You know, someone new, but...

22:43.144 --> 22:45.451
it-it's not about that.

22:49.106 --> 22:52.109
Then what is it about?
Is it, like, a...

22:52.109 --> 22:54.024
a co-parenting arrangement

22:54.111 --> 22:55.461
- or...
- No. I, uh...

22:57.463 --> 22:59.247
I want to be a family.

23:02.119 --> 23:03.599
I want us to be a family.

23:05.601 --> 23:08.256
I mean, look at Lottie.

23:08.343 --> 23:10.476
I mean, she's fucking amazing.

23:12.478 --> 23:15.263
She's the physical manifestation
of what happens

23:15.263 --> 23:17.004
when we get together.

23:17.047 --> 23:19.223
I mean, she's smart,

23:19.267 --> 23:22.226
she's kind, she's sensitive,
and she's intuitive.

23:22.270 --> 23:24.054
- Mm-hmm.
- She's...

23:24.141 --> 23:27.101
the best... parts of

23:27.144 --> 23:28.842
both of us. I'm just...

23:31.497 --> 23:32.454
I...

23:32.498 --> 23:35.501
I know you love Lottie, and...

23:37.372 --> 23:39.766
...I know you'll miss her.

23:42.246 --> 23:44.335
I'm fighting for you, Van.

23:44.379 --> 23:46.076
You know me.
I don't fight for anything.

23:51.081 --> 23:52.866
Van, look at me.

23:57.958 --> 23:59.438
I love you.

24:05.095 --> 24:07.402
I can't just pack up
my whole life

24:07.489 --> 24:08.577
'cause you love me
as Lottie's mom.

24:16.193 --> 24:17.760
That's not...

24:17.760 --> 24:19.762
enough...

24:19.849 --> 24:21.329
for me.

24:41.741 --> 24:43.699
Do you think I just
see you as Lottie's mom?

24:46.354 --> 24:49.183
Do you not realize how...

24:49.226 --> 24:50.837
in love with you I am?

24:54.493 --> 24:56.930
How much I think about you?

25:01.891 --> 25:04.154
I've dreamed about you
every night since Amsterdam.

25:08.245 --> 25:12.032
I do see you as a woman.

25:12.119 --> 25:15.209
I still want you.

25:15.252 --> 25:17.167
I desire you, Van.

25:24.697 --> 25:26.612
When I think about
the fact that...

25:26.699 --> 25:29.179
that you are also
the mother of my child...

25:35.577 --> 25:36.622
...I could just fucking burst.

25:39.059 --> 25:42.628
I've never felt that way
about anything.

25:42.628 --> 25:44.630
I wasn't able...

25:44.630 --> 25:46.762
I wasn't able
to feel that before.

25:49.199 --> 25:51.288
And I'll love you forever

25:51.288 --> 25:53.116
because of that, no matter what.

26:00.210 --> 26:02.212
I mean, what else
are we doing this for...

26:04.301 --> 26:07.174
...if not for that feeling?

26:07.217 --> 26:08.654
What else is there?

26:08.741 --> 26:09.785
You know what I mean?

26:13.746 --> 26:15.312
I do.

26:18.315 --> 26:20.666
It's... a little...

26:22.319 --> 26:23.843
...Kanye being passionate,

26:23.886 --> 26:26.149
but I do know what you mean.

26:40.033 --> 26:42.470
I don't want to find
someone new.

26:42.557 --> 26:45.342
Not because it's...

26:45.342 --> 26:48.650
it isn't time-consuming, and...

26:48.694 --> 26:50.783
you know, annoying,

26:50.826 --> 26:53.350
which it is.

26:53.437 --> 26:54.830
It's because...

26:57.703 --> 27:00.401
I... I just want
to do this with you.

27:05.145 --> 27:07.713
Okay? I just want
to do this with you.

27:10.237 --> 27:13.022
Will you go to L.A. with me,

27:13.066 --> 27:14.720
so we can be a family?

27:18.288 --> 27:19.594
Like, a for-real family?

27:28.081 --> 27:30.387
Okay... Okay.

27:33.652 --> 27:35.044
Okay.

27:40.397 --> 27:41.660
Are you cold?

27:43.270 --> 27:45.228
- Yeah, I'm freezing.
- Okay.

28:03.203 --> 28:05.684
I love you, too.

28:07.903 --> 28:09.122
I know.

28:11.864 --> 28:13.126
I know.

28:15.215 --> 28:16.433
Me too.

28:41.807 --> 28:43.722
I think there's a slant.

28:51.468 --> 28:53.862
I think we slid down.

29:09.486 --> 29:10.749
Mm!

29:12.272 --> 29:13.403
Now you spit.

29:16.624 --> 29:18.582
Supposed to rain today.

29:18.626 --> 29:21.063
What?

29:21.063 --> 29:22.848
When?

29:32.596 --> 29:35.208
Leave it.
We'll-we'll get another.

29:37.514 --> 29:41.127
Okay. Come on.

29:41.170 --> 29:43.520
- Baby, come on, let's go.
- Yeah, let's get in the car.

29:49.875 --> 29:51.441
- Got it?
- Yeah.

